# Release V080 -- Restore Overdue Recalls (correct process definition)
# =====================================================================
# Overdue Recalls was wrongly removed in the recall rebuild. It IS a valid metric -- a PRACTICE
# PROCESS backlog: recalls that are DUE but the practice has not actioned (open/Unbooked, past
# due, NO reminder sent). Nothing to do with the old buggy due-date-derived count (3,126) that
# swept in completed cycles.
#
#   * usp_Load_Fact_Metric_Actuals: dropped overdue_recalls from the (buggy) KPI-snapshot #snp read;
#     compute it fresh -- Fact_Recalls Status='Unbooked' AND Is_Reminder_Sent=0 AND Due_Date<=today.
#     Dev T100: 148 recalls (was 3,126).
#   * Config.Metric_Definitions: overdue_recalls reactivated (Is_Active=1) + redefined.
#
# C# (NOT a warehouse deploy): TabularEditor_Patients.csx (restored measure + card) +
# TabularEditor_MetricActuals.csx (overdue_recalls -> 'cur' mapping) -- re-apply + refresh.
#
# Deploy AFTER V078. Idempotent (DROP/CREATE SP + MERGE catalog).
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V080__restore_overdue_recalls.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY  Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Fact_Metric_Actuals.StoredProcedure.sql
